IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgc1-s201-departures`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), s 201(1) to (11) (Part 6, Division 1): the directors' duty to lay financial statements, what they must contain,
-- the steps before they are made out, their audit, the definition of "financial statements" in (8) and (9), the ultimate parent corporation.
-- Subsections (3), (4) and (6) are shown deleted (Act 15 of 2017). (12) to (15A) are in sgc1-s201-departures.l4, (16) to (23) in sgc1-s201-statement.l4.
-- "Parent company" and "subsidiary company" are defined for this Part in s 209A (another part's, and by reference to the Accounting Standards, not s 5):
-- each is taken as an input named for the fact.

§ `Section 201: the acts of the regulative rules of subsections (1) to (11)`

DECLARE `s 201 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 201(1) lay the financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting`
    `s 201(5) cause to be made out and lay the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet of the parent company`
    `s 201(7) take the reasonable steps as to bad debts, current assets and non-current assets`
    `s 201(9)(a) take reasonable steps to ensure that the financial statements are audited as required`
    `s 201(9)(b) cause the auditor's report to be attached to the financial statements`
    `s 201(11) state the name of the ultimate parent corporation in the financial statements`

§ `Section 201(1): the financial statements to be laid`

-- src:17928 | Financial statements and consolidated financial statements
-- src:17930 | 201.—(1) The directors of every company must lay before the
-- src:17931 | company at its annual general meeting the financial statements for the
-- src:17932 | financial year in respect of which the annual general meeting is held.
@ref s 201(1) (src:17928-17932)
GIVEN `the financial statements are for the financial year in respect of which the annual general meeting is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(1) the financial statements are the ones the directors must lay before the company at its annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the financial statements are for the financial year in respect of which the annual general meeting is held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names "the financial statements for the financial year in respect of which the annual general meeting is held" and says nothing of statements for another year

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The time the text gives is the meeting itself ("lay before the company at its annual general meeting"):
-- the clock counts days from the start of the trace, and the meeting falls `the number of days from now until the annual general meeting` days on.
@ref s 201(1) (src:17930-17932)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from now until the annual general meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201 act`
`s 201(1) the directors of a company must lay the financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201(1) lay the financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now until the annual general meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the financial statements were not laid before the company at its annual general meeting"

§ `Section 201(2): what the financial statements must be like`

-- Subsection (5) puts the same two requirements on the consolidated financial statements and on the parent company's balance sheet ("each of which
-- complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards and gives a true and fair view"), so this one function serves for all three documents.
-- src:17936 | (2) Subject to subsections (12) to (15A), the financial statements
-- src:17937 | mentioned in subsection (1) must comply with the requirements of
-- src:17938 | the Accounting Standards and give a true and fair view of the
-- src:17939 | financial position and performance of the company.
@ref s 201(2) (src:17936-17939)
GIVEN `the document complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document gives a true and fair view of the financial position and performance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a departure from the Accounting Standards is allowed by subsection (12), (13) or (15A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(2) the document complies with the Accounting Standards and gives a true and fair view` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document gives a true and fair view of the financial position and performance`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the financial statements ... must ... give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the company" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)
    ELSE IF `the document complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `a departure from the Accounting Standards is allowed by subsection (12), (13) or (15A)`
              WHEN JUST allowed THEN JUST allowed   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must comply with the requirements of the Accounting Standards" (where no departure is allowed under subsections (12) to (15A) the duty stands, and the answer is the allowance function's own JUST FALSE)
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a departure is allowed is not decided by the facts given

§ `Section 201(5): the directors of a parent company`

-- src:17952 | (5) Subject to subsections (12) to (15A), the directors of a company
-- src:17953 | that is a parent company at the end of its financial year need not
-- src:17954 | comply with subsection (1) but must cause to be made out and laid
-- src:17955 | before the company at its annual general meeting —
-- src:17957 | (a) consolidated financial statements dealing with the
-- src:17958 | financial position and performance of the group for the
-- src:17959 | financial year in respect of which the annual general
-- src:17960 | meeting is held; and
-- src:17962 | (b) a balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the
-- src:17963 | parent company at the end of its financial year,
-- src:17965 | each of which complies with the requirements of the Accounting
-- src:17966 | Standards and gives a true and fair view of the matters referred to in
-- src:17967 | paragraph (a) or (b) (as the case may be) so far as it concerns
-- src:17968 | members of the parent company.
@ref s 201(5) (src:17952-17968)
GIVEN `the company is a parent company at the end of its financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(5) the directors need not comply with subsection (1) but must lay the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet` MEANS
    IF `the company is a parent company at the end of its financial year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a company that is a parent company at the end of its financial year" and says nothing of any other company (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

@ref s 201(5) (src:17952-17968)
GIVEN `the company is a parent company at the end of its financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consolidated financial statements comply with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consolidated financial statements give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the balance sheet complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the balance sheet gives a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the parent company at the end of its financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a departure from the Accounting Standards is allowed by subsection (12), (13) or (15A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(5) the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet are as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a parent company at the end of its financial year`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a company that is a parent company at the end of its financial year" and says nothing of any other company
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 201(2) the document complies with the Accounting Standards and gives a true and fair view` `the consolidated financial statements comply with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` `the consolidated financial statements give a true and fair view of the financial position and performance of the group` `a departure from the Accounting Standards is allowed by subsection (12), (13) or (15A)`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each of which complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards and gives a true and fair view" (the consolidated financial statements fail: a duty not met)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a departure is allowed is not decided by the facts given
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 201(2) the document complies with the Accounting Standards and gives a true and fair view` `the balance sheet complies with the requirements of the Accounting Standards` `the balance sheet gives a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the parent company at the end of its financial year` `a departure from the Accounting Standards is allowed by subsection (12), (13) or (15A)`

@ref s 201(5) (src:17952-17968)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from now until the annual general meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201 act`
`s 201(5) the directors of a parent company must cause to be made out and lay the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201(5) cause to be made out and lay the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet of the parent company`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now until the annual general meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet were not laid before the company at its annual general meeting"

§ `Section 201(7): the reasonable steps before the financial statements are made out`

-- src:17976 | (7) The directors must (before the financial statements mentioned
-- src:17977 | in subsection (1) and the balance sheet mentioned in subsection (5)(b)
-- src:17978 | are made out) take reasonable steps —
-- src:17980 | (a) to ascertain what action has been taken in relation to the
-- src:17981 | writing off of bad debts and the making of provisions for
-- src:17982 | doubtful debts and to cause all known bad debts to be
-- src:17983 | written off and adequate provision to be made for doubtful
-- src:17984 | debts;
@ref s 201(7)(a) (src:17976-17984)
GIVEN `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain what action has been taken in relation to the writing off of bad debts and the making of provisions for doubtful debts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause all known bad debts to be written off and adequate provision to be made for doubtful debts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(7)(a) the directors have taken the reasonable steps as to bad debts and doubtful debts` MEANS
    IF    `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain what action has been taken in relation to the writing off of bad debts and the making of provisions for doubtful debts`
       AND `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause all known bad debts to be written off and adequate provision to be made for doubtful debts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must ... take reasonable steps — (a) to ascertain what action has been taken in relation to the writing off of bad debts ... and to cause all known bad debts to be written off and adequate provision to be made for doubtful debts" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- The time the text gives is "before the financial statements ... are made out": the clock counts days from the start of the trace.
@ref s 201(7) (src:17976-17984)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from now until the financial statements are made out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201 act`
`s 201(7) the directors must take reasonable steps before the financial statements are made out` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201(7) take the reasonable steps as to bad debts, current assets and non-current assets`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now until the financial statements are made out`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not take the reasonable steps required before the financial statements were made out"

-- src:17986 | (b) to ascertain whether any current assets (other than current
-- src:17987 | assets to which paragraph (a) applies) are unlikely to
-- src:17988 | realise in the ordinary course of business their value as
-- src:17989 | shown in the accounting records of the company and, if so,
-- src:17990 | to cause —
-- src:17992 | (i) those assets to be written down to an amount which
-- src:17993 | they might be expected so to realise; or
-- src:17995 | (ii) adequate provision to be made for the difference
-- src:17996 | between the amount of the value as so shown and the
-- src:17997 | amount that they might be expected so to realise; and
@ref s 201(7)(b) (src:17986-17997)
GIVEN `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain whether any current assets (other than current assets to which paragraph (a) applies) are unlikely to realise in the ordinary course of business their value as shown in the accounting records of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some such current assets are unlikely to realise in the ordinary course of business their value as shown in the accounting records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause those assets to be written down to an amount which they might be expected so to realise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause adequate provision to be made for the difference between the amount of the value as so shown and the amount that they might be expected so to realise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(7)(b) the directors have taken the reasonable steps as to current assets` MEANS
    IF    `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain whether any current assets (other than current assets to which paragraph (a) applies) are unlikely to realise in the ordinary course of business their value as shown in the accounting records of the company`
       AND (    (NOT `some such current assets are unlikely to realise in the ordinary course of business their value as shown in the accounting records`)
             OR `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause those assets to be written down to an amount which they might be expected so to realise`
             OR `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause adequate provision to be made for the difference between the amount of the value as so shown and the amount that they might be expected so to realise`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to ascertain whether any current assets ... are unlikely to realise in the ordinary course of business their value as shown in the accounting records of the company and, if so, to cause — (i) those assets to be written down ...; or (ii) adequate provision to be made for the difference" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- src:18002 | (c) to ascertain whether any non‑current asset is shown in the
-- src:18003 | books of the company at an amount which, having regard
-- src:18004 | to its value to the company as a going concern, exceeds the
-- src:18005 | amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or
-- src:18006 | on its disposal and (unless adequate provision for writing
-- src:18007 | down that asset is made) to cause to be included in the
-- src:18008 | financial statements such information and explanations as
-- src:18009 | will prevent the financial statements from being
-- src:18010 | misleading by reason of the overstatement of the amount
-- src:18011 | of that asset.
@ref s 201(7)(c) (src:18002-18011)
GIVEN `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain whether any non-current asset is shown in the books of the company at an amount which, having regard to its value to the company as a going concern, exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some non-current asset is shown at an amount which exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adequate provision for writing down that asset has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause to be included in the financial statements such information and explanations as will prevent the financial statements from being misleading by reason of the overstatement of the amount of that asset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(7)(c) the directors have taken the reasonable steps as to non-current assets` MEANS
    IF    `the directors have taken reasonable steps to ascertain whether any non-current asset is shown in the books of the company at an amount which, having regard to its value to the company as a going concern, exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal`
       AND (    (NOT `some non-current asset is shown at an amount which exceeds the amount which would be recoverable over its useful life or on its disposal`)
             OR `adequate provision for writing down that asset has been made`
             OR `the directors have taken reasonable steps to cause to be included in the financial statements such information and explanations as will prevent the financial statements from being misleading by reason of the overstatement of the amount of that asset`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to ascertain whether any non-current asset is shown in the books of the company at an amount which ... exceeds the amount which would be recoverable ... and (unless adequate provision for writing down that asset is made) to cause to be included in the financial statements such information and explanations" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Section 201(8): the audit`

-- src:18015 | (8) The financial statements must be duly audited before they are
-- src:18016 | laid before the company at its annual general meeting as required by
-- src:18017 | this section, and the auditor’s report required by section 207 must be
-- src:18018 | attached to or endorsed upon those financial statements.
@ref s 201(8) (src:18015-18018)
GIVEN `the financial statements are duly audited before they are laid before the company at its annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor's report required by section 207 is attached to or endorsed upon the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(8) the financial statements have been audited and reported on as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the financial statements are duly audited before they are laid before the company at its annual general meeting`
       AND `the auditor's report required by section 207 is attached to or endorsed upon the financial statements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The financial statements must be duly audited before they are laid before the company at its annual general meeting ..., and the auditor's report required by section 207 must be attached to or endorsed upon those financial statements" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

§ `Section 201(9): the audit not less than 14 days before the meeting, and the auditor's report`

-- src:18022 | (9) The directors of the company must —
-- src:18024 | (a) take reasonable steps to ensure that the financial statements
-- src:18025 | are audited as required by this Part not less than 14 days
-- src:18026 | before the annual general meeting of the company, unless
-- src:18027 | all the persons entitled to receive notice of general
-- src:18028 | meetings of the company agree that the financial
-- src:18029 | statements may be audited as required by this Part less
-- src:18030 | than 14 days before the annual general meeting of the
-- src:18031 | company; and
-- src:18033 | (b) cause to be attached to those financial statements the
-- src:18034 | auditor’s report that is furnished to the directors under
-- src:18035 | section 207(1A).
@ref s 201(9) (src:18022-18035)
GIVEN `the date of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree that the financial statements may be audited less than 14 days before the annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 201(9)(a) the latest day by which the financial statements are to be audited` MEANS
    IF `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree that the financial statements may be audited less than 14 days before the annual general meeting`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree that the financial statements may be audited ... less than 14 days before the annual general meeting": once they agree the paragraph fixes no latest day
    ELSE JUST (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date of the annual general meeting` 14 Days)

@ref s 201(9)(a) (src:18022-18031)
GIVEN `the date of the annual general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the day the audit of the financial statements is completed` IS A DATE
      `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree that the financial statements may be audited less than 14 days before the annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(9)(a) the financial statements have been audited in time` MEANS
    IF `all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree that the financial statements may be audited less than 14 days before the annual general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the audit of the financial statements is completed` `the date of the annual general meeting` 14 Days
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "take reasonable steps to ensure that the financial statements are audited as required by this Part not less than 14 days before the annual general meeting of the company, unless all the persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company agree" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

@ref s 201(9)(a) (src:18022-18031)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from now until the latest day by which the financial statements are to be audited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201 act`
`s 201(9)(a) the directors must take reasonable steps to ensure that the financial statements are audited not less than 14 days before the annual general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201(9)(a) take reasonable steps to ensure that the financial statements are audited as required`
    WITHIN `the number of days from now until the latest day by which the financial statements are to be audited`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not take reasonable steps to ensure that the financial statements were audited not less than 14 days before the annual general meeting"

@ref s 201(9)(b) (src:18033-18035)
GIVEN `the auditor's report that is furnished to the directors under section 207(1A) is attached to the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(9)(b) the directors have caused the auditor's report to be attached` MEANS
    IF `the auditor's report that is furnished to the directors under section 207(1A) is attached to the financial statements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of the company must — ... (b) cause to be attached to those financial statements the auditor's report that is furnished to the directors under section 207(1A)" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the paragraph: no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201(9)(b) (src:18033-18035)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201 act`
`s 201(9)(b) the directors must cause the auditor's report to be attached to the financial statements` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201(9)(b) cause the auditor's report to be attached to the financial statements`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not cause the auditor's report to be attached to the financial statements" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

§ `Section 201(10): what "financial statements" means in subsections (8) and (9)`

DECLARE `s 201(10) the documents meant by financial statements` IS ONE OF
    `s 201(10)(a) the financial statements required to be laid under subsection (1)`
    `s 201(10)(b) the consolidated financial statements of the group and the balance sheet of the parent company required to be laid under subsection (5)`

-- src:18039 | (10) In subsections (8) and (9), “financial statements”, in relation to
-- src:18040 | a company, means —
-- src:18042 | (a) in the case where the company is not a parent company —
-- src:18043 | the financial statements required to be laid before the
-- src:18044 | company at its annual general meeting under
-- src:18045 | subsection (1); or
-- src:18050 | (b) in the case where the company is a parent company — the
-- src:18051 | consolidated financial statements of the group and the
-- src:18052 | balance sheet of the parent company required to be laid
-- src:18053 | before the company at its annual general meeting under
-- src:18054 | subsection (5).
@ref s 201(10) (src:18039-18054)
GIVEN `the company is a parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 201(10) the documents meant by financial statements`
`s 201(10) the documents that "financial statements" means in subsections (8) and (9)` MEANS
    IF `the company is a parent company`
    THEN `s 201(10)(b) the consolidated financial statements of the group and the balance sheet of the parent company required to be laid under subsection (5)`
    ELSE `s 201(10)(a) the financial statements required to be laid under subsection (1)`

§ `Section 201(11): the ultimate parent corporation`

-- src:18058 | (11) Where at the end of a financial year a company is the
-- src:18059 | subsidiary company of another corporation, the directors of the
-- src:18060 | company must state in, or in a note as a statement annexed to, the
-- src:18061 | financial statements laid before the company at its annual general
-- src:18062 | meeting the name of the corporation which is its ultimate parent
-- src:18063 | corporation.
@ref s 201(11) (src:18058-18063)
GIVEN `at the end of the financial year the company is a subsidiary company of another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(11) the directors must state the name of the ultimate parent corporation` MEANS
    IF `at the end of the financial year the company is a subsidiary company of another corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where at the end of a financial year a company is the subsidiary company of another corporation, the directors of the company must state ..." (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

@ref s 201(11) (src:18058-18063)
GIVEN `at the end of the financial year the company is a subsidiary company of another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements laid before the company at its annual general meeting state, in the statements or in a note as a statement annexed to them, the name of the corporation which is its ultimate parent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(11) the directors have stated the name of the ultimate parent corporation` MEANS
    IF NOT `at the end of the financial year the company is a subsidiary company of another corporation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a company that "is the subsidiary company of another corporation" at the end of the financial year
    ELSE IF `the financial statements laid before the company at its annual general meeting state, in the statements or in a note as a statement annexed to them, the name of the corporation which is its ultimate parent corporation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors of the company must state in, or in a note as a statement annexed to, the financial statements laid before the company at its annual general meeting the name of the corporation which is its ultimate parent corporation" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection: no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201(11) (src:18058-18063)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201 act`
`s 201(11) the directors of a subsidiary company must state the name of its ultimate parent corporation` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201(11) state the name of the ultimate parent corporation in the financial statements`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not state the name of the ultimate parent corporation in the financial statements" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
